  "source": "Seaboard Marine (sbmar.com) \u2014 advisory operating ranges, NOT factory alarm setpoints",
  "notes": "Cummins does not publish QSB 6.7 setpoints; they are in the operator's manual and QuickServe. Every band here is a green advisory range with a citation, and raises no alarm. The warn and alarm thresholds are deliberately unset - fill them from your manual and they become real alarms. Path suffixes were verified against a live QSB 6.7 vessel: the engine temperature is `temperature` (not `coolantTemperature`), the only oil temperature is the gearbox's `transmission.oilTemperature`, and exhaust temperature is published under `propulsion.0`/`propulsion.1` rather than the engine node, so no suffix can reach it - add it by hand. propulsion.<id>.fuel.economy is deliberately not included: it is per engine, so on a twin it reads roughly twice the boat's actual figure. Bind helmcentral.propulsion.fuelEconomy for the vessel's own economy instead.",
